    feeds: ["generativity", "meaning", "resilience"],
    description:
      "Generativity — caring for and contributing to the next generation — is measurable through self-report, acts and narrative themes, and midlife adults higher in generativity report better psychosocial adaptation; in older age it is part of what successful ageing means. Posttraumatic growth is the popular idea that loss produces growth, and meta-analysis links reported benefit-finding to less depression and more well-being. The honest boundary is a prospective study that found self-reported growth after trauma did not track actual change in the same domains, and a conceptual review that treats growth as possible rather than expected. The protocol builds generativity through action and lets any 'growth' be a by-product rather than a demand.",
